# .gitignore — reproduction bundle
#
# The Kaggle API token does NOT live in this repository.  It sits at the project
# root, one level above every git tree here, and the checked history of this
# repository contains zero occurrences of its value.  The rules below are a
# second line of defence, not the first.  If a token ever does reach a commit,
# editing this file will not remove it: the history has to be rewritten and the
# token reissued at once.

# --- secrets: the part that matters ---
.env
*.env
.envrc
kaggle
kaggle.*
.kaggle/
credentials.json
client_secret*.json
service-account*.json
*.token
*_token*
*.pem
*.key
*.pfx
*.p12
.netrc
_netrc
id_rsa*
secrets.*

# --- data: generated by scripts, not tracked ---
data/raw/
data/processed/
data/interim/
data/external/
# training/data/*.npz IS tracked: dataset_generation.py generates it, and the
# experiments need it to reproduce anything without a retraining run.
!data/checksums.sha256
!data/README.md

# --- weights and checkpoints: deliberately NOT ignored ---
# code/checkpoints is 1.1 MB across eight files, far under any limit, and a
# reproduction bundle whose weights live somewhere else stops reproducing on the
# day that somewhere else moves.  The same files also go into the Zenodo
# deposit, which is the archival copy rather than a replacement for this one.
# What IS ignored here is the noise a training run leaves behind:
runs/
wandb/
mlruns/
lightning_logs/
tensorboard/
outputs/

# --- Python ---
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*$py.class
.venv/
venv/
env/
.python-version
build/
dist/
*.egg-info/
.eggs/
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.tox/
.nox/
.coverage
.coverage.*
htmlcov/
.ipynb_checkpoints/
.hypothesis/

# --- editors: both ignored on purpose ---
# PyCharm writes absolute interpreter paths into .idea/ and VS Code writes them
# into .vscode/settings.json.  Committed, they break the moment a co-author on
# another machine opens the project, and they are the usual way a local absolute
# path with a user name in it becomes public.
.idea/
*.iml
.vscode/
*.code-workspace
.history/
*.swp
*.swo
*~

# --- OS ---
.DS_Store
._*
Thumbs.db
ehthumbs.db
desktop.ini
$RECYCLE.BIN/
*.lnk

# --- LaTeX ---
*.aux
*.log
*.out
*.toc
*.lof
*.lot
*.blg
*.bcf
*.run.xml
*.nav
*.snm
*.vrb
*.synctex.gz
*.fdb_latexmk
*.fls
*.xdv
*.figlist
*.makefile
# *.bbl is NOT ignored: arXiv requires it in the package, it does not run bibtex.
# These two logs are evidence, not build noise, so they survive the *.log rule
# above — negations must come after the pattern they undo.
!train_b4.log
!train_log.txt

# --- run artefacts ---
# written while a long probe run is in flight, replaced when it lands
*.json.partial
*.tmp

# --- the withdrawn first version: kept on disk, out of the branch ---
# latex/ holds the LaTeX source, figures and PDF of the first version of this
# work, titled "Separating physical particle heating from numerical drift in
# non-stationary magnetic fields", which was withdrawn.  Its figures are not the
# figures of the present paper and its numbers are not the numbers of the
# present paper.  Nothing under code/ reads it, so it adds nothing reproducible
# and a reader who opens it finds a different title over different figures.
# Untracked in 2026-09; it remains in the history before that commit, which is
# deliberate — several reports cite commit hashes, and rewriting the history
# would break those references.
latex/
